  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Is My Home Really Safe for Aging In Place?",
    "text": "Is My Home Really Safe for Aging In Place?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "It's natural to wonder if your home is truly set up for long-term independent living. Often, the biggest concerns revolve around fall hazards, adequate lighting, and making sure the bathroom is safe. Think about your entry and exit points too — are they easy to navigate? What about clutter, or your readiness for emergencies? These are all super important questions to ask. A lot of folks don't realize how small issues can become big problems later on, so a fresh set of eyes can really help. If you're spotting a few potential issues or just want peace of mind, getting a professional senior home safety assessment is a smart move. They can pinpoint those hidden risks and suggest practical, actionable fixes to make your home safer and more comfortable for years to come. This way, you're not guessing; you're getting expert advice.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
